cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use PixPoint in a publication, please cite it as below and the papers behind the estimators you used (see the Citing page of the documentation)."
type: software
title: "PixPoint: correlation functions of HEALPix maps on GPUs and CPUs"
abstract: "PixPoint measures two-point, three-point, integrated three-point and one-point statistics of cosmological fields on HEALPix maps (cosmic shear, galaxy clustering, galaxy-galaxy lensing, convergence). The pixel pairs of a footprint are found once and reused for every map; measurements run on CPUs via Numba and on NVIDIA GPUs via CuPy."
authors:
  - family-names: Gebauer
    given-names: David
    email: git@gebauer.ai
    affiliation: "Ludwig-Maximilians-Universität München, University Observatory"
repository-code: "https://github.com/D-Gebauer/PixPoint"
url: "https://pixpoint.readthedocs.io"
license: MIT
keywords:
  - cosmology
  - weak lensing
  - galaxy clustering
  - correlation functions
  - three-point functions
  - HEALPix
  - GPU
